<onlyinclude>'''Metaphysics''' is a branch of philosophy investigating fundamental questions about what exists and the nature and structure of reality. Topics include identity, causation, time, possibility, properties and relations.

== Explanation ==
For example, metaphysicians ask what makes an object the same object over time, whether possibilities are real in some sense, and what it means for one thing to cause another. These questions involve conceptual analysis, arguments and engagement with scientific findings. Metaphysics is not synonymous with supernatural belief.

